WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.450
Welcome to Module 5 Reasoning with SQL Logic Earlier
modules focused on

00:00:05.462 --> 00:00:10.700
retrieving rows changing data safely and creating
summaries Now we focus on

00:00:10.725 --> 00:00:13.775
the rules that decide which rows qualify and how
values should be

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:19.062
classified Real data is not always simple conditions
overlap fields may be

00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:23.212
missing and SQL can produce an UNKNOWN truth state
We will work

00:00:23.225 --> 00:00:28.012
with AND OR and NOT then study TRUE FALSE and
UNKNOWN We

00:00:28.025 --> 00:00:31.888
will use NULL-safe tools such as IS NULL IS DISTINCT
FROM COALESCE

00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:35.512
and NULLIF and we will build CASE expressions where
branch order matters

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.750
The main habit is to reason before writing syntax
state the rule

00:00:39.888 --> 00:00:43.462
decide how missing values should behave write the
SQL and test edge

00:00:43.475 --> 00:00:43.975
cases
